## Conclusion — delivery 2 accepted
The assembled delivery game-developer@e2970e952cdb0273617ac41c547a0d3cb3c81502 + artist@b2daa7038200d3e5c5c85a5bae323c40fafb319b is the game the input asks for. It is Pong in the browser, one player against a computer opponent, with the player's paddle on the keyboard and first to 5 winning. It has a title screen, a live score, and a result screen naming the winner with play again. R1–R8 were each observed by my own play, QA's checks and the playtest, with no open defect.

Open, non-blocking:
- The centre line crosses "GET READY" during the serve pause.
- Difficulty depends on how the player plays: anticipating players win easily, ball-chasing players lose.
- Audio has been verified by file inspection and load/play without errors, but no one has judged it by ear.
